title: 'statement-store: drop peers that left the network from the DHT index'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    On the v2 DHT path a peer that left the network no longer stays in the DHT index. Discovery
    events named such a peer long after it left and kept restarting its two-hour eviction time.
    Now only an identify answer or an open statement substream of the peer restarts it. The choice
    of the peers that cover the node's own topics passes over an unreachable peer and takes
    another replica of the topic, and it prefers a connected replica.
crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
